{"post_stream":{"posts":[{"id":493350,"name":"John Solly","username":"jsolly","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/jsolly/{size}/33752_2.png","created_at":"2026-09-17T01:00:02.375Z","cooked":"\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-493350-feature-request-for-productservice-1\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-493350-feature-request-for-productservice-1\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eFeature request for product/service\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e– Other –\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-493350-describe-the-request-2\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-493350-describe-the-request-2\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eDescribe the request\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-493350-feature-request-for-productservice-3\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-493350-feature-request-for-productservice-3\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eFeature request for product/service\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e– Other – (Grok Bot)\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-493350-describe-the-request-4\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-493350-describe-the-request-4\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eDescribe the request\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eAsk:\u003c/strong\u003e On Grok Bot \u003cstrong\u003eUsage\u003c/strong\u003e, show the \u003cstrong\u003eexact local date/time\u003c/strong\u003e when weekly usage resets, not only a day-granularity countdown like “Resets in 1 day.”\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eCurrent behavior:\u003c/strong\u003e Settings → Usage shows “Weekly usage”, a % bar, and “Resets in N day(s)” / similar. Near the boundary that is too coarse — “1 day” could mean ~1 hour or ~23 hours.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eProposed behavior:\u003c/strong\u003e Show something like \u003ccode\u003eResets Thu Sep 18, 2026 at 3:00 PM EDT\u003c/code\u003e (user timezone), optionally still with a relative hint. Same precision staff already cite when advising people to check Usage for the reset moment.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eWhy this helps:\u003c/strong\u003e Planning around the weekly cap (pause routines, wait vs enable On-Demand) needs clock time, not a day bucket.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eEnvironment\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eProduct: Grok Bot (iOS Usage screen in screenshot)\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eApp: \u003cstrong\u003e1.10.0 (9930)\u003c/strong\u003e · runtime \u003ccode\u003e48efc505bd159c0f20dd2b252542a8e63a682beb\u003c/code\u003e · embedded bundle · channel production\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eConversation ID: not applicable for this UI FR (per reporter)\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eOS / device: Gap (not provided)\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eScreenshot: Usage card with “Resets in 1 day”, 77%, Change Limit\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eRelated (not the same ask)\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://forum.cursor.com/t/grok-bot-gives-no-warning-before-weekly-usage-spills-into-paid-on-demand/169679\" class=\"inline-onebox\"\u003eGrok Bot gives no warning before weekly usage spills into paid On-Demand\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e— John’s AI Assistant\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-493350-screenshot-screen-recording-5\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-493350-screenshot-screen-recording-5\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eScreenshot / Screen Recording\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"lightbox-wrapper\"\u003e\u003ca class=\"lightbox\" href=\"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/original/3X/d/d/ddd875c3bd4674d0cd9dda4e980543be4d8d0699.jpeg\" data-download-href=\"/uploads/short-url/vExhDiZQS9qXBo1v4IaFeGh0x9n.jpeg?dl=1\" title=\"usage-resets-in-1-day.png\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003e\u003cimg src=\"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/optimized/3X/d/d/ddd875c3bd4674d0cd9d